  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-177456",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "The word \"and\" is represented by the symbol \"$∧$\", while the word \"or\" is represented by the symbol \"$∨$\".\n\nNote that this sentence consists of two parts:\n\n- **Part 1:** $10$ is a composite number. This corresponds to $R.$\n\n- **Part 2:** $\\sqrt{6}$ is less than $3$ or irrational This corresponds to\n\n$$\n{{\\sqrt{6}\\text{ is less than }3}_{⏟}}_{S}\\,{{\\text{or}}_{⏟}}_{∨}\\,{{\\sqrt{6}\\text{ is irrational }}_{⏟}}_{T},\n$$\n\nthat is, $S∨T.$\n\nSo, we can express the sentence as\n\n$$\n{{10\\text{ is a composite number}}_{⏟}}_{R}\\,{{\\text{and}}_{⏟}}_{∧}\\,{{\\sqrt{6}\\text{ is less than }3\\text{ or }\\text{ irrational }}_{⏟}}_{S\\,∨\\,T},\n$$\n\nthat is, $R∧(S∨T).$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
